(3299534, 454246, 70661, '<td valign="top">I really liked this.</td>', 'I really liked this.', '2007-01-29 16:13:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299562, 456318, 62095, '<td valign="top">Quck Quack Quack!<br/> <br/>Great shot, really active. The motion blur adds to the photo. I think perhaps a bit under-rated.  To top it off something really different in the frame would have provided contrast and a focal point.</td>', 'Quck Quack Quack! Great shot, really active. The motion blur adds to the photo. I think perhaps a bit under-rated.  To top it off something really different in the frame would have provided contrast and a focal point.', '2007-01-29 16:20:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299567, 455539, 62095, '<td valign="top">Great score for this shot, well deserved.  The parallel lines of the bills are impressive, almost made for a photo.</td>', 'Great score for this shot, well deserved.  The parallel lines of the bills are impressive, almost made for a photo.', '2007-01-29 16:21:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299572, 454780, 62095, '<td valign="top">The pose here is certainly different to the usual, so you''re going for out of the box territory, but it''s difficult for my eyes to find a resting point on the image, because I''m expecting to see a different angle of the bird.</td>', 'The pose here is certainly different to the usual, so you''re going for out of the box territory, but it''s difficult for my eyes to find a resting point on the image, because I''m expecting to see a different angle of the bird.', '2007-01-29 16:23:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299584, 456542, 62095, '<td valign="top">A good sky and a good idea for the challenge, but I think it scored lower than it should have because the contrast with the birds is not as high as it might be.  If they stood out more it would be a winner.</td>', 'A good sky and a good idea for the challenge, but I think it scored lower than it should have because the contrast with the birds is not as high as it might be.  If they stood out more it would be a winner.', '2007-01-29 16:24:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299589, 456752, 62095, '<td valign="top">I like here how the birds are all in different yet complimentory phases of wing-stretch.</td>', 'I like here how the birds are all in different yet complimentory phases of wing-stretch.', '2007-01-29 16:25:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299597, 455681, 62095, '<td valign="top">I''m not entirely sure that I agree with the too dark comments here, only a small part of the animals'' fronts are dark on my screen.  Would probably have been a difficult shot to meter, too, what with the contrast.</td>', 'I''m not entirely sure that I agree with the too dark comments here, only a small part of the animals'' fronts are dark on my screen.  Would probably have been a difficult shot to meter, too, what with the contrast.', '2007-01-29 16:27:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299602, 456696, 62095, '<td valign="top">Yeah. Personally I think it''s a well-toned and detailed shot, but you were always going to get killed by the strict DNMC crowd. Shame.</td>', 'Yeah. Personally I think it''s a well-toned and detailed shot, but you were always going to get killed by the strict DNMC crowd. Shame.', '2007-01-29 16:29:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299608, 455988, 62095, '<td valign="top">So close to a 6, really deserved one I think for this shot. Maybe you hit the camera''s limits with the sharpness as focus looks on to me and the bokeh fits nicely and blends well.</td>', 'So close to a 6, really deserved one I think for this shot. Maybe you hit the camera''s limits with the sharpness as focus looks on to me and the bokeh fits nicely and blends well.', '2007-01-29 16:30:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299616, 456004, 62095, '<td valign="top">I think this is a great shot. The timing is good, and the colours are well-captured. The only thing that takes away from it in my view is the one bird top-right that is way in the foreground compared to the others in that section of the shot.  Were it not for that bird I think it would be even better.</td>', 'I think this is a great shot. The timing is good, and the colours are well-captured. The only thing that takes away from it in my view is the one bird top-right that is way in the foreground compared to the others in that section of the shot.  Were it not for that bird I think it would be even better.', '2007-01-29 16:32:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299623, 455640, 62095, '<td valign="top">Great job here.  The b&amp;w conversion with the selective colour works well with the texture and level of sharpness that you have captured.</td>', 'Great job here.  The b&w conversion with the selective colour works well with the texture and level of sharpness that you have captured.', '2007-01-29 16:34:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299628, 456769, 62095, '<td valign="top">This is a fantastic shot with an eerie quality to it. Quality job.</td>', 'This is a fantastic shot with an eerie quality to it. Quality job.', '2007-01-29 16:35:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299645, 453762, 62095, '<td valign="top">I think for this I would have had to go one way or the other with the depth of field.  Either drop down and attempt to bring the duck in to focus, or push the focus further away.  As it is my eyes are drawn back and forward in an awkward manner. The general composition though is outstanding.</td>', 'I think for this I would have had to go one way or the other with the depth of field.  Either drop down and attempt to bring the duck in to focus, or push the focus further away.  As it is my eyes are drawn back and forward in an awkward manner. The general composition though is outstanding.', '2007-01-29 16:37:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299650, 454256, 62095, '<td valign="top">Wow what a concept.  Great, new and interesting point of view, and a fluffily artistic background too.</td>', 'Wow what a concept.  Great, new and interesting point of view, and a fluffily artistic background too.', '2007-01-29 16:38:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299652, 456772, 62095, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot of the little guy.  I think shallow DOF shots tend to underscore on here really.</td>', 'This is a great shot of the little guy.  I think shallow DOF shots tend to underscore on here really.', '2007-01-29 16:39:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299711, 456002, 42567, '<td valign="top">Sandy this is awesome!  I gave you a 10!  Its a shame to get a score 7 and be out of the top 10!  Great picture and capture.  I couldn''t imagine seeing something like this in the wild much like take a great picture like this.  Way to go!  Congratulations</td>', 'Sandy this is awesome!  I gave you a 10!  Its a shame to get a score 7 and be out of the top 10!  Great picture and capture.  I couldn''t imagine seeing something like this in the wild much like take a great picture like this.  Way to go!  Congratulations', '2007-01-29 16:50:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299718, 455785, 42567, '<td valign="top">This is way cool!  Great detail and focus.  Very tough challenge!</td>', 'This is way cool!  Great detail and focus.  Very tough challenge!', '2007-01-29 16:51:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299767, 455890, 24962, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 10, was there any other score worthy!! Great photo!</td>', 'I gave this a 10, was there any other score worthy!! Great photo!', '2007-01-29 16:59:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299775, 455658, 24962, '<td valign="top">I looked at this and then looked again, was it a 9 or a 10. The stag, such a noble subject...gave it 10!</td>', 'I looked at this and then looked again, was it a 9 or a 10. The stag, such a noble subject...gave it 10!', '2007-01-29 17:01:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299896, 456306, 65319, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your Top 10 placement.  I actually thought the fox picture might be yours because of your recent ribbon winning cat picture which I loved!  This wildlife photo of the deer is so outstanding...!!!  Your contribution to this horse race made this challenge incredibly exciting to watch!  I was very suprised this photo didn''t make into the Top 3.</td>', 'Congratulations on your Top 10 placement.  I actually thought the fox picture might be yours because of your recent ribbon winning cat picture which I loved!  This wildlife photo of the deer is so outstanding...!!!  Your contribution to this horse race made this challenge incredibly exciting to watch!  I was very suprised this photo didn''t make into the Top 3.', '2007-01-29 17:29:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299976, 455881, 50695, '<td valign="top">I''m afraid you have an interesting picture that doesn''t look like all the other bird pictures in the challenge, so I''ll give you a low score and offer some tips on how to be completely conventional...</td>', 'I''m afraid you have an interesting picture that doesn''t look like all the other bird pictures in the challenge, so I''ll give you a low score and offer some tips on how to be completely conventional...', '2007-01-29 17:46:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299977, 455658, 16739, '<td valign="top">Only 9 votes 5 and under, Thats fantastic</td>', 'Only 9 votes 5 and under, Thats fantastic', '2007-01-29 17:46:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299980, 455890, 44534, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  This picture is outstanding, it looks as though the fox could jump out of the screen!! I really like this one!</td>', 'Congratulations!  This picture is outstanding, it looks as though the fox could jump out of the screen!! I really like this one!', '2007-01-29 17:47:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3299987, 455890, 3575, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your win and such an incredible photo!</td>', 'Congratulations on your win and such an incredible photo!', '2007-01-29 17:49:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300016, 456511, 5112, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot, Jason.  Congratulations on the high score in this very hard challenge.</td>', 'Beautiful shot, Jason.  Congratulations on the high score in this very hard challenge.', '2007-01-29 17:55:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300019, 456306, 5112, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your high placement and score!</td>', 'Congratulations on your high placement and score!', '2007-01-29 17:56:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300075, 455658, 23203, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, you''re on a roll!</td>', 'Congratulations, you''re on a roll!', '2007-01-29 18:11:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300076, 455658, 36988, '<td valign="top">Outstanding work Alex. Totally worthy of such an honored standing amongst the sites very best.</td>', 'Outstanding work Alex. Totally worthy of such an honored standing amongst the sites very best.', '2007-01-29 18:11:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300081, 456767, 36988, '<td valign="top">Very, very cool image. Great job in a very tough challenge.</td>', 'Very, very cool image. Great job in a very tough challenge.', '2007-01-29 18:12:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300094, 456767, 23203, '<td valign="top">Awesome! This is national geographic worthy!<br/></td>', 'Awesome! This is national geographic worthy!', '2007-01-29 18:15:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300139, 456767, 40667, '<td valign="top">very cool... love your comments on the photo!</td>', 'very cool... love your comments on the photo!', '2007-01-29 18:29:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300146, 455658, 29949, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon! This is an AMAZING shot! once i saw it i cannot look away from it!</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon! This is an AMAZING shot! once i saw it i cannot look away from it!', '2007-01-29 18:31:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300150, 455890, 19978, '<td valign="top">This shot deservedly takes its place in the DPC hall of fame. I keep returning to gaze at it every time I see the front page of the site. What an accomplishment!</td>', 'This shot deservedly takes its place in the DPC hall of fame. I keep returning to gaze at it every time I see the front page of the site. What an accomplishment!', '2007-01-29 18:32:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300266, 455658, 32997, '<td valign="top">stunning...what beautiful work!</td>', 'stunning...what beautiful work!', '2007-01-29 19:11:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300275, 455068, 32997, '<td valign="top">this shot really stands out...great composition, love the reflection...</td>', 'this shot really stands out...great composition, love the reflection...', '2007-01-29 19:16:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300296, 455890, 18339, '<td valign="top">I''m so happy for you!!! A beautiful photo, the blue and an amazing score! You deserve every bit of it :)</td>', 'I''m so happy for you!!! A beautiful photo, the blue and an amazing score! You deserve every bit of it :)', '2007-01-29 19:26:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300314, 456002, 39184, '<td valign="top">Hey Sandy, I just now got a chance to sit down and start going through the lineup post-contest.  I remember this shot from the beginning as one of the ones that I thought was going to do really well.  Nice crop, nice dark background, and great shot overall.  My son, ''yakatyou'' sitting next to me asked me to say that he likes it too.  Actually, he was looking specifically for this entry to see where it placed.</td>', 'Hey Sandy, I just now got a chance to sit down and start going through the lineup post-contest.  I remember this shot from the beginning as one of the ones that I thought was going to do really well.  Nice crop, nice dark background, and great shot overall.  My son, ''yakatyou'' sitting next to me asked me to say that he likes it too.  Actually, he was looking specifically for this entry to see where it placed.', '2007-01-29 19:32:13.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(3300317, 455881, 35357, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m afraid you have an interesting picture that doesn''t look like all the other bird pictures in the challenge, so I''ll give you a low score and offer some tips on how to be completely conventional... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Haha!</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: I''m afraid you have an interesting picture that doesn''t look like all the other bird pictures in the challenge, so I''ll give you a low score and offer some tips on how to be completely conventional...  Haha!', '2007-01-29 19:33:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300379, 456445, 28172, '<td valign="top">I want to thank everyone for the really nice comments! This was one very competitive challenge and there were fantastic images by a lot of great photographers.  I am humbled to be among them.  Wow!  I especially want to thank my dear friend "hihosilver" for finding a spectacular location to photograph pelicans and for being so encouraging and patient with the unending amount of images I send to her daily for her opinion.</td>', 'I want to thank everyone for the really nice comments! This was one very competitive challenge and there were fantastic images by a lot of great photographers.  I am humbled to be among them.  Wow!  I especially want to thank my dear friend "hihosilver" for finding a spectacular location to photograph pelicans and for being so encouraging and patient with the unending amount of images I send to her daily for her opinion.', '2007-01-29 19:53:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300381, 455462, 48389, '<td valign="top">Nice position in the frame and I love how we can see the birds feet, really interesting but as some of your commenters have said it could do with being a little sharper. Not the easiest thing to photograph and get tack sharp though! :o)</td>', 'Nice position in the frame and I love how we can see the birds feet, really interesting but as some of your commenters have said it could do with being a little sharper. Not the easiest thing to photograph and get tack sharp though! :o)', '2007-01-29 19:54:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300404, 455890, 31637, '<td valign="top">OH WOW ! Rare photo of such a beautiful canine.</td>', 'OH WOW ! Rare photo of such a beautiful canine.', '2007-01-29 20:03:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300411, 455890, 61222, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your First Blue, this is amazing capture. He even has a sly look in his eyes. Perfect image. :-)</td>', 'Congratulations on your First Blue, this is amazing capture. He even has a sly look in his eyes. Perfect image. :-)', '2007-01-29 20:06:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300509, 455820, 8367, '<td valign="top">Excellent capture! Thanks for posting your in depth Photographer''s comments.</td>', 'Excellent capture! Thanks for posting your in depth Photographer''s comments.', '2007-01-29 20:32:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300535, 455890, 46177, '<td valign="top">I just have to jump in here and say thank you again, I can''t believe these comments they are so amazing and I appreciate everyone of them! It was a freezing cold day when I got this shot and the hours spent in the cold were definately all worth it.  A Big thanks to all again!!<br/>Sue</td>', 'I just have to jump in here and say thank you again, I can''t believe these comments they are so amazing and I appreciate everyone of them! It was a freezing cold day when I got this shot and the hours spent in the cold were definately all worth it.  A Big thanks to all again!!Sue', '2007-01-29 20:38:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300544, 455890, 39588, '<td valign="top">This STUNS ME!!!<br/> <br/>oh wow.<br/>brilliant.<br/> <br/>Just... totally perfect!<br/> <br/>ayyy!<br/>I''ve never seen a real live fox before =[</td>', 'This STUNS ME!!! oh wow.brilliant. Just... totally perfect! ayyy!I''ve never seen a real live fox before =[', '2007-01-29 20:40:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300612, 455890, 28172, '<td valign="top">I love this shot and I am glad that you got the blue!  I love the wonderful expression of this fox.  The lighting is fantastic and the detail and sharpness are just great!</td>', 'I love this shot and I am glad that you got the blue!  I love the wonderful expression of this fox.  The lighting is fantastic and the detail and sharpness are just great!', '2007-01-29 20:54:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300653, 456318, 40973, '<td valign="top">Such a fun photograph-I look at the duck faces and imagine what they''re saying to each other. Love the colors and chaos.</td>', 'Such a fun photograph-I look at the duck faces and imagine what they''re saying to each other. Love the colors and chaos.', '2007-01-29 20:59:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300659, 454780, 23484, '<td valign="top">Julianne, This has really good DOF and very well composed. The only thing that I''m not sure of is the background. The colors just seem a little washed out. I''m not sure why. It''s still a nice shot. I gave it a 6.</td>', 'Julianne, This has really good DOF and very well composed. The only thing that I''m not sure of is the background. The colors just seem a little washed out. I''m not sure why. It''s still a nice shot. I gave it a 6.', '2007-01-29 21:00:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300664, 455890, 60846, '<td valign="top">good job</td>', 'good job', '2007-01-29 21:03:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300676, 456696, 23484, '<td valign="top">This is a very interesting shot.  What I like most is the effect that the processing has on the surrounding snow.  I don''t know if the lighting is from the processing or natural but I like the way it tightly surrounds the foot print.</td>', 'This is a very interesting shot.  What I like most is the effect that the processing has on the surrounding snow.  I don''t know if the lighting is from the processing or natural but I like the way it tightly surrounds the foot print.', '2007-01-29 21:05:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300688, 456318, 66597, '<td valign="top">Raish,<br/>I found this to be an interesting shot. I''ve never seen such a large congregation of ducks in one spot! It almost has the feeling of an abstract. The motion in the beaks works well.</td>', 'Raish,I found this to be an interesting shot. I''ve never seen such a large congregation of ducks in one spot! It almost has the feeling of an abstract. The motion in the beaks works well.', '2007-01-29 21:07:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300699, 456542, 66597, '<td valign="top">Jayson,<br/>I like the patterns in the clouds a lot, as I think they are a nice foil to the pure black silhouettes of the birds. The composition is also interesting. I think this could be enhanced with a frame to pull it all together. Think this one is underrated - the more I look at it the more it grows on me.</td>', 'Jayson,I like the patterns in the clouds a lot, as I think they are a nice foil to the pure black silhouettes of the birds. The composition is also interesting. I think this could be enhanced with a frame to pull it all together. Think this one is underrated - the more I look at it the more it grows on me.', '2007-01-29 21:10:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300704, 456542, 40973, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote in this challenge but looked through the thumbnails and thought this one was stunning. Delighted that it was a team suck entry! The gold sky works for me - makes what might have been a stereotype sunset -much more interesting.</td>', 'I didn''t vote in this challenge but looked through the thumbnails and thought this one was stunning. Delighted that it was a team suck entry! The gold sky works for me - makes what might have been a stereotype sunset -much more interesting.', '2007-01-29 21:10:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300705, 456752, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very nice simple shot. This just give me a feeling of serenity when I look at it. Maybe it''s just the soft almost pastel colors in the sky.</td>', 'Very nice simple shot. This just give me a feeling of serenity when I look at it. Maybe it''s just the soft almost pastel colors in the sky.', '2007-01-29 21:11:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300717, 455681, 23484, '<td valign="top">Very nice capture.  I like the way they are interacting with each other. I just wish it were a bit sharper. I gave it a 6 but if it were sharper, it would have easily been a 7 in my book.</td>', 'Very nice capture.  I like the way they are interacting with each other. I just wish it were a bit sharper. I gave it a 6 but if it were sharper, it would have easily been a 7 in my book.', '2007-01-29 21:14:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300724, 455681, 66597, '<td valign="top">Very expressive, great capture. I agree with skewsme that lightening them up a notch would help them "pop" via more details. The eye always tends to be drawn to the brightest thing in the frame, and in this case it is the snow behind the deer. You have all the right elements here, just a difficult lighting situation, in which either fill-flash on site or corrections in PS might render a result you liked even more.</td>', 'Very expressive, great capture. I agree with skewsme that lightening them up a notch would help them "pop" via more details. The eye always tends to be drawn to the brightest thing in the frame, and in this case it is the snow behind the deer. You have all the right elements here, just a difficult lighting situation, in which either fill-flash on site or corrections in PS might render a result you liked even more.', '2007-01-29 21:16:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300727, 456769, 23484, '<td valign="top">Really nice capture. You did an excellent job on this one. It almost looks like a painting that would be hanging on the wall of a hunting lodge. I gave it a 7.</td>', 'Really nice capture. You did an excellent job on this one. It almost looks like a painting that would be hanging on the wall of a hunting lodge. I gave it a 7.', '2007-01-29 21:17:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300736, 455988, 66597, '<td valign="top">I was quite taken with this shot - I love the sense of the frog curled up in all that green - it gives me a cozy feeling for some reason. I think this is a very good photo indeed, just a very tough challenge. You should be proud of a great capture like this!</td>', 'I was quite taken with this shot - I love the sense of the frog curled up in all that green - it gives me a cozy feeling for some reason. I think this is a very good photo indeed, just a very tough challenge. You should be proud of a great capture like this!', '2007-01-29 21:19:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300740, 455681, 40973, '<td valign="top">Snow is actually difficult to deal with in photos that''s why there are so many grey or blue snow photos from underexposure. But you mastered a snow shot. The exposure of the snow is good-white snow. I enjoy the way the deer/elk are going about their meal but casting a careful eye your way.</td>', 'Snow is actually difficult to deal with in photos that''s why there are so many grey or blue snow photos from underexposure. But you mastered a snow shot. The exposure of the snow is good-white snow. I enjoy the way the deer/elk are going about their meal but casting a careful eye your way.', '2007-01-29 21:20:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300757, 456004, 66597, '<td valign="top">Even as I voted, I was reminded of Melethia''s abstract pigeons, but thought it surely was a coincidence manufactured by my pointy little brain. But no - it was intentional, after all! Frankly the two photos would look excellent hanging in tandem in a little gallery somewhere. Deb''s reminds me of whirling bits of Swedish glass, and yours reminds me of flying pieces of bronze and gold. It''s the contrast in seeming weight and heft that make these two photos so interesting to me on a side-by-side basis. Anyway, love them both.</td>', 'Even as I voted, I was reminded of Melethia''s abstract pigeons, but thought it surely was a coincidence manufactured by my pointy little brain. But no - it was intentional, after all! Frankly the two photos would look excellent hanging in tandem in a little gallery somewhere. Deb''s reminds me of whirling bits of Swedish glass, and yours reminds me of flying pieces of bronze and gold. It''s the contrast in seeming weight and heft that make these two photos so interesting to me on a side-by-side basis. Anyway, love them both.', '2007-01-29 21:25:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300759, 455966, 53964, '<td valign="top">I suspect that most of the comments about quality all boil down to having to zoooooooooooom, right? :)<br/>Because, knowing where that was shot, I suspect he was in one of those trees on the land side, not peninsula side? I''ve taken eagle shots down there that ended up almost exactly the same!<br/>I still like it though... it''s not easy to get a good shot of these ugly mugs :D</td>', 'I suspect that most of the comments about quality all boil down to having to zoooooooooooom, right? :)Because, knowing where that was shot, I suspect he was in one of those trees on the land side, not peninsula side? I''ve taken eagle shots down there that ended up almost exactly the same!I still like it though... it''s not easy to get a good shot of these ugly mugs :D', '2007-01-29 21:25:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300768, 456696, 40973, '<td valign="top">A deer? I thought it was BigFoot or the Jersey Devil! Aren''t the comments fun when voters are confused?</td>', 'A deer? I thought it was BigFoot or the Jersey Devil! Aren''t the comments fun when voters are confused?', '2007-01-29 21:28:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300776, 455640, 66597, '<td valign="top">Darren,<br/>Congrats on that killer score! My new goal is to hit 6.5, and you beat me to the punch. Good on ya mate, as I believe your countryman say? Please forgive me if I erroneously borrowed that expression. The sentiment remains the same: super score on an intriguing photo. One of the few instances of someone pulling off selective desat without a lot of backlash. And BTW - look at that average from the commenters! You''ve got a fan club! :-)</td>', 'Darren,Congrats on that killer score! My new goal is to hit 6.5, and you beat me to the punch. Good on ya mate, as I believe your countryman say? Please forgive me if I erroneously borrowed that expression. The sentiment remains the same: super score on an intriguing photo. One of the few instances of someone pulling off selective desat without a lot of backlash. And BTW - look at that average from the commenters! You''ve got a fan club! :-)', '2007-01-29 21:30:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300790, 456767, 23430, '<td valign="top">This was my favourite shot in this challenge. I love your subject and the close and interesting POV. Congrats on getting the YELLOW ribbon and such a high score.</td>', 'This was my favourite shot in this challenge. I love your subject and the close and interesting POV. Congrats on getting the YELLOW ribbon and such a high score.', '2007-01-29 21:33:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300791, 456733, 41047, '<td valign="top">tebrikler! real good capture.</td>', 'tebrikler! real good capture.', '2007-01-29 21:33:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300794, 454256, 66597, '<td valign="top">You caught this goose at an unusual angle, and certainly did a good job of focusing on the goose''s considerable heft - keeping in line with your title "Another Sucker to Feed Me." I''m glad you included the straw in the background, as it adds interest and depth. I''m a little confused about the relationship of the bright blue area in the snow. One trick I''ve done to finish a lot of wildlife shots is to dodge the area just around the eye to make it pop (not too much, or it looks fake) but enough to draw attention.</td>', 'You caught this goose at an unusual angle, and certainly did a good job of focusing on the goose''s considerable heft - keeping in line with your title "Another Sucker to Feed Me." I''m glad you included the straw in the background, as it adds interest and depth. I''m a little confused about the relationship of the bright blue area in the snow. One trick I''ve done to finish a lot of wildlife shots is to dodge the area just around the eye to make it pop (not too much, or it looks fake) but enough to draw attention.', '2007-01-29 21:35:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300802, 455988, 40973, '<td valign="top">Kelli, Your zoo shots are so amazing. The green color and the diagonal postion are great. Your subject-the frog-is in focus. The branch in front is softly focused but that is part of a shallow depth of field and is fine with me.</td>', 'Kelli, Your zoo shots are so amazing. The green color and the diagonal postion are great. Your subject-the frog-is in focus. The branch in front is softly focused but that is part of a shallow depth of field and is fine with me.', '2007-01-29 21:38:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300820, 456767, 31341, '<td valign="top">Super shot.  Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'Super shot.  Congrats on the ribbon!', '2007-01-29 21:42:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300824, 455890, 31341, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon!  The lighting makes this one jump out at me!</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon!  The lighting makes this one jump out at me!', '2007-01-29 21:43:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300842, 455640, 40973, '<td valign="top">You can do my portrait anytime - if you can make a goat look that good - I can imagine what you could do for an elderly lady wrinkles and all.<br/> <br/>I love everything about this - the high contrast between the goat and background, the detail in the fur(?), and of course the eye.<br/> <br/></td>', 'You can do my portrait anytime - if you can make a goat look that good - I can imagine what you could do for an elderly lady wrinkles and all. I love everything about this - the high contrast between the goat and background, the detail in the fur(?), and of course the eye. ', '2007-01-29 21:49:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300873, 454015, 3569, '<td valign="top">I agree fox sparrow, I haven''t seen that race since I left Oregon and forgot how mush yellow is on their bill. I was thinking European species.   Great shot.  Van</td>', 'I agree fox sparrow, I haven''t seen that race since I left Oregon and forgot how mush yellow is on their bill. I was thinking European species.   Great shot.  Van', '2007-01-29 21:57:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300883, 455890, 20462, '<td valign="top">Honestly, who doesn''t love foxes (except some grumpy farmers).  This one, obviously, is very nice.  The angle is a little bizarre though.  Amazingly, I think this could have been a touch better with a better vantage point...</td>', 'Honestly, who doesn''t love foxes (except some grumpy farmers).  This one, obviously, is very nice.  The angle is a little bizarre though.  Amazingly, I think this could have been a touch better with a better vantage point...', '2007-01-29 22:00:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300888, 454256, 40973, '<td valign="top">I feel like I''m having a face-to-face talk with this goose. To me that the goose pretty much dominates and fills the frame distracts me from noticing the snow so much. I don''t think you screwed up.</td>', 'I feel like I''m having a face-to-face talk with this goose. To me that the goose pretty much dominates and fills the frame distracts me from noticing the snow so much. I don''t think you screwed up.', '2007-01-29 22:01:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300892, 456544, 30049, '<td valign="top">Hey.  That''s pretty cool, getting a shot with them all together like that.  We have the same mix around here, but they''re usually pretty well spread out in the main (birdfeeder) tree and surrounding bushes.<br/> <br/>Hope you didn''t get your camera wet!  :P</td>', 'Hey.  That''s pretty cool, getting a shot with them all together like that.  We have the same mix around here, but they''re usually pretty well spread out in the main (birdfeeder) tree and surrounding bushes. Hope you didn''t get your camera wet!  :P', '2007-01-29 22:02:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300919, 456770, 61559, '<td valign="top">"Yes, it''s a zoo shot. So sue me."<br/> <br/>I think it''s a real shame that a Site Council member would engage in such a blatantly poor display of sportsmanship.</td>', '"Yes, it''s a zoo shot. So sue me." I think it''s a real shame that a Site Council member would engage in such a blatantly poor display of sportsmanship.', '2007-01-29 22:08:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300928, 456767, 7842, '<td valign="top">I LOVE this shot!  I am always bringing my camera w/me kayking trying to capture what you did.  GREAT JOB!</td>', 'I LOVE this shot!  I am always bringing my camera w/me kayking trying to capture what you did.  GREAT JOB!', '2007-01-29 22:11:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300953, 456002, 64571, '<td valign="top">Awesome, Sandy!  Congrats on your finish :)</td>', 'Awesome, Sandy!  Congrats on your finish :)', '2007-01-29 22:14:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3300997, 456770, 17203, '<td valign="top">Zoo shots were within the rules and fared well in Wildlife I and Wildlife II without complaint. Considering the time and effort I spent in sub-zero wind chills to get this, I would hardly call it poor sportsmanship to poke fun at myself.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-29 22:24:24.</i></td>', 'Zoo shots were within the rules and fared well in Wildlife I and Wildlife II without complaint. Considering the time and effort I spent in sub-zero wind chills to get this, I would hardly call it poor sportsmanship to poke fun at myself.', '2007-01-29 22:23:45.000000', '2007-01-29 22:24:24.000000', 0),
(3301033, 455539, 66384, '<td valign="top">Even though I think it looks a little over-saturated, I gave this a 9 because it is such a terrific composition. I love the parallel diagonal lines of the bills. Congratulations on a very nice photo and a very nice score.</td>', 'Even though I think it looks a little over-saturated, I gave this a 9 because it is such a terrific composition. I love the parallel diagonal lines of the bills. Congratulations on a very nice photo and a very nice score.', '2007-01-29 22:33:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301109, 456770, 61559, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scalvert:</b></div><hr/><i> Zoo shots were within the rules and fared well in Wildlife I and Wildlife II without complaint. Considering the time and effort I spent in sub-zero wind chills to get this, I would hardly call it poor sportsmanship to poke fun at myself. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>"...living in a natural environment." That''s a direct copy from the description. A zoo is NOT a natural environment, no matter how you want to rationalize and twist it.<br/> <br/>That''s not poking fun at yourself, it''s a slap in everyone else''s face. "Ha. Look at me! I''m on the Site Council, I can make up rules as I go along! Nanananana!!!"<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by scalvert: Zoo shots were within the rules and fared well in Wildlife I and Wildlife II without complaint. Considering the time and effort I spent in sub-zero wind chills to get this, I would hardly call it poor sportsmanship to poke fun at myself.   "...living in a natural environment." That''s a direct copy from the description. A zoo is NOT a natural environment, no matter how you want to rationalize and twist it. That''s not poking fun at yourself, it''s a slap in everyone else''s face. "Ha. Look at me! I''m on the Site Council, I can make up rules as I go along! Nanananana!!!" ', '2007-01-29 22:50:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301113, 454930, 42567, '<td valign="top">Great picture!  Congratulations on a great score and finish!</td>', 'Great picture!  Congratulations on a great score and finish!', '2007-01-29 22:52:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301140, 455640, 42826, '<td valign="top">i think you were robbed in this one...but that''s a personal opinion!</td>', 'i think you were robbed in this one...but that''s a personal opinion!', '2007-01-29 23:00:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301297, 453762, 62318, '<td valign="top">I think overall the mood is great. It is a very artisticly done shot. I don''t mind the depth choice used here, I think having the front duck slightly out of focus works great.  There are just a few compositional elements I would change, and really this is mostly beyond your control. The ducks in the pond, I wish they were more to the left, or at least the two to the furthest to the right. They distract just a bit from the front ducks form. It would just be a small element that would make a better line and get more involement in that middle section. Lastly just a slight adjustment in the angle, maybe just a bit higher, so you could get the foreground duck''s head in the water rather than covering up some elements in the background. Granted of course that you can still maintain the same general perspective <br/> <br/>However, I''m just picking on very small details here. It''s the type of thing that makes a great wildlife picture extrodinary. Sometimes a little luck has to come into play. Wildlife I think is the hardest, because in the purest sense you have the lease amount of control of your subjects. This is really a tremendous photo you have here!</td>', 'I think overall the mood is great. It is a very artisticly done shot. I don''t mind the depth choice used here, I think having the front duck slightly out of focus works great.  There are just a few compositional elements I would change, and really this is mostly beyond your control. The ducks in the pond, I wish they were more to the left, or at least the two to the furthest to the right. They distract just a bit from the front ducks form. It would just be a small element that would make a better line and get more involement in that middle section. Lastly just a slight adjustment in the angle, maybe just a bit higher, so you could get the foreground duck''s head in the water rather than covering up some elements in the background. Granted of course that you can still maintain the same general perspective  However, I''m just picking on very small details here. It''s the type of thing that makes a great wildlife picture extrodinary. Sometimes a little luck has to come into play. Wildlife I think is the hardest, because in the purest sense you have the lease amount of control of your subjects. This is really a tremendous photo you have here!', '2007-01-29 23:26:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301356, 456770, 17203, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rob_banks:</b></div><hr/><i>"Ha. Look at me! I''m on the Site Council, I can make up rules as I go along! Nanananana!!!" </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The challenge description is not a rule. Your own "At the Beach" entry was all water, when the challenge description clearly defined beach as <i>the strip of land</i> bordering the water. Did you break the rules? No.</td>', 'Originally posted by rob_banks:"Ha. Look at me! I''m on the Site Council, I can make up rules as I go along! Nanananana!!!"   The challenge description is not a rule. Your own "At the Beach" entry was all water, when the challenge description clearly defined beach as the strip of land bordering the water. Did you break the rules? No.', '2007-01-29 23:50:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301389, 456002, 41337, '<td valign="top">You''re my inspiration! Bummer that this fell out of the top 10. Still deserves that star.</td>', 'You''re my inspiration! Bummer that this fell out of the top 10. Still deserves that star.', '2007-01-29 23:59:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3301431, 456770, 61559, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scalvert:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rob_banks:</b></div><hr/><i>"Ha. Look at me! I''m on the Site Council, I can make up rules as I go along! Nanananana!!!" </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The challenge description is not a rule. Your own "At the Beach" entry was all water, when the challenge description clearly defined beach as <i>the strip of land</i> bordering the water. Did you break the rules? No. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''re right. My FIRST ENTRY did not include the actual beach in the photo and I learned from my mistake. The rules said "Go to the beach and photograph what you find..." Because I could see the wakeboarder from the beach, I felt it fit the Challenge description, took my lumps and tried to learn from my experience. Ditto, the B &amp; W Portrait Challenge. I took a picture of a horse (portrait seems to mean "person" to a lot of people) and I''m sure many people downgraded it as a result. That''s why it scored a bit lower despite having one more favorite. <br/> <br/>You, on the other hand, are on the Site Council, have been her a LONG time and obviously "get it" because you''ve won quite a few awards. <br/> <br/>I guess it''s going to be awhile before I "get it" if I decide to keep competing. Just because "see" is a synonym for "find," it doesn''t mean you can replace it in the description. Portrait means person. Thinking out of the box is bad. Check all the old challenges if it''s a sequel. <br/> <br/>Oh yeah. The Description is only a Description, it''s not a rule, except when the VOTERS think it''s a rule, THEN it''s a rule!<br/> <br/>And, by your reasoning, if the guy that took the picture of the STUFFED Canadian Lynx had won, he still wins. Be sure and visit the taxidermist for Wildlife IV.</td>', 'Originally posted by scalvert: Originally posted by rob_banks:"Ha. Look at me! I''m on the Site Council, I can make up rules as I go along! Nanananana!!!"   The challenge description is not a rule. Your own "At the Beach" entry was all water, when the challenge description clearly defined beach as the strip of land bordering the water. Did you break the rules? No.   You''re right. My FIRST ENTRY did not include the actual beach in the photo and I learned from my mistake. The rules said "Go to the beach and photograph what you find..." Because I could see the wakeboarder from the beach, I felt it fit the Challenge description, took my lumps and tried to learn from my experience. Ditto, the B & W Portrait Challenge. I took a picture of a horse (portrait seems to mean "person" to a lot of people) and I''m sure many people downgraded it as a result. That''s why it scored a bit lower despite having one more favorite.  You, on the other hand, are on the Site Council, have been her a LONG time and obviously "get it" because you''ve won quite a few awards.  I guess it''s going to be awhile before I "get it" if I decide to keep competing. Just because "see" is a synonym for "find," it doesn''t mean you can replace it in the description. Portrait means person. Thinking out of the box is bad. Check all the old challenges if it''s a sequel.  Oh yeah. The Description is only a Description, it''s not a rule, except when the VOTERS think it''s a rule, THEN it''s a rule! And, by your reasoning, if the guy that took the picture of the STUFFED Canadian Lynx had won, he still wins. Be sure and visit the taxidermist for Wildlife IV.', '2007-01-30 00:18:47.000000', NULL, 0),
