(3307558, 456197, 47933, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club Paul!<br/> <br/>Congrats on your highest score and good placement in the challenge. <br/> <br/>Overall I''d consider this to be a fine shot. The focus is dead on the face/eyes where you want it and your placement of the subject in the frame was nicely done. I also like the vertical portrait style rather than landscape for this one.<br/> <br/>I can see by your camera settings that you were shooting under poor conditions. I think if the light would''ve cooperated to allow you to shut down the aperture to get more depth of field you''d have fared even better in the challenge. The background is great but the out of focus limb in front is a bit distracting. I realize that the limb isn''t the main subject but it does grab my attention. <br/> <br/>Like I said before, an overall good shot indeed.<br/> <br/>Cheers - Phil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Paul! Congrats on your highest score and good placement in the challenge.  Overall I''d consider this to be a fine shot. The focus is dead on the face/eyes where you want it and your placement of the subject in the frame was nicely done. I also like the vertical portrait style rather than landscape for this one. I can see by your camera settings that you were shooting under poor conditions. I think if the light would''ve cooperated to allow you to shut down the aperture to get more depth of field you''d have fared even better in the challenge. The background is great but the out of focus limb in front is a bit distracting. I realize that the limb isn''t the main subject but it does grab my attention.  Like I said before, an overall good shot indeed. Cheers - Phil', '2007-01-31 10:52:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3308225, 456446, 62925, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nullix:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow, my first brown ribbin.  Thanks for the comments all.  No thanks to the, "DNMC" comments.  I live in California, we don''t have wildlife.<br/> <br/>Special props to the people who got the Steve Erwin and Latin references. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>..i took my shot in California :P</td>', 'Originally posted by Nullix: Wow, my first brown ribbin.  Thanks for the comments all.  No thanks to the, "DNMC" comments.  I live in California, we don''t have wildlife. Special props to the people who got the Steve Erwin and Latin references.   ..i took my shot in California :P', '2007-01-31 13:04:52.000000', NULL, 0),
