(3316463, 456752, 62318, '<td valign="top">I actually like how you shot this underexposed. Maybe even a half a stop more underexposer to really bring out those textured clouds. Very simple composition but works. I like how the birds are flying into the frame. Wonderful colors. The simple line the birds make are great. I had this one rated much higher than your final. I think the problem with this picture it takes a few minutes to appreciate, it is pretty easy to overlook on a quick glance.</td>', 'I actually like how you shot this underexposed. Maybe even a half a stop more underexposer to really bring out those textured clouds. Very simple composition but works. I like how the birds are flying into the frame. Wonderful colors. The simple line the birds make are great. I had this one rated much higher than your final. I think the problem with this picture it takes a few minutes to appreciate, it is pretty easy to overlook on a quick glance.', '2007-02-01 23:26:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3316502, 455988, 62318, '<td valign="top">I must be weird, everyone else likes the greens, I am not a fan. Too much competition from that background green. For me, it just doesn''t seem to gel. I''ve heard that men see green different than women, maybe that is it. :)<br/> <br/>Beyond that though, everything else is terrific. The way you framed the frog is nice. I also like the textures going on here. Exposure is great. It is a terrific shot though. Your eye goes aroudn the whole frame smoothly. Nice job on the placement and a well deserved score!</td>', 'I must be weird, everyone else likes the greens, I am not a fan. Too much competition from that background green. For me, it just doesn''t seem to gel. I''ve heard that men see green different than women, maybe that is it. :) Beyond that though, everything else is terrific. The way you framed the frog is nice. I also like the textures going on here. Exposure is great. It is a terrific shot though. Your eye goes aroudn the whole frame smoothly. Nice job on the placement and a well deserved score!', '2007-02-01 23:32:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3316526, 456769, 62318, '<td valign="top">This was one of the standout''s for me in the challenge. I really like what you captured here. The wolf is amazing. I think it is funny you commented on the bokeh, that was the only thing that was out of place when I voted. I wasn''t quite sure what it was. No biggie, still a great photo. I like the subdued clolrs and the nice contrast in the wolf. Excellent shot! Congrats on the high ranking.</td>', 'This was one of the standout''s for me in the challenge. I really like what you captured here. The wolf is amazing. I think it is funny you commented on the bokeh, that was the only thing that was out of place when I voted. I wasn''t quite sure what it was. No biggie, still a great photo. I like the subdued clolrs and the nice contrast in the wolf. Excellent shot! Congrats on the high ranking.', '2007-02-01 23:34:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3316952, 456767, 36619, '<td valign="top">congrats on your first ribbon!</td>', 'congrats on your first ribbon!', '2007-02-02 00:44:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3318139, 455640, 60862, '<td valign="top">Holy cow!  Errrr ... Holy goat!  Fantastic shot, love the eye and the composition.  I''m sorry for your not meeting your predictions.  That''s what you get for creating a great image that''s in focus. ;)</td>', 'Holy cow!  Errrr ... Holy goat!  Fantastic shot, love the eye and the composition.  I''m sorry for your not meeting your predictions.  That''s what you get for creating a great image that''s in focus. ;)', '2007-02-02 10:26:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3318174, 456542, 60862, '<td valign="top">This is really great.  Then again, I love pure silhouettes.</td>', 'This is really great.  Then again, I love pure silhouettes.', '2007-02-02 10:39:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3319571, 456767, 56015, '<td valign="top">A ribbon well deserved for such a stunning close-up, If I was shooting this, I would be up in a balloon with a remote switch.</td>', 'A ribbon well deserved for such a stunning close-up, If I was shooting this, I would be up in a balloon with a remote switch.', '2007-02-02 16:45:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3319718, 456553, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, this is a strong picture.  The bird is located roughly on the upper right third and this gives a sense of balance to the shot.  Also, while this location of the subject can sometimes feel out of balance, the fact that the bird is flying "into" the frame helps.  The negative space gives the sense of freedom that one can sometimes associate with birds.<br/> <br/>Technically, the shot is focus and exposed well.  The colors are simple, so they aren''t distracting, and the bird shows up well on the blue sky.  I do notice a couple of streaks, and after reading your notes, I''m wondering if it is where you cloned out your powerlines.  In normal voting, I''m not sure I would have noticed it, but in studying the picture to critique it, I can''t miss it, and now when I glance at the shot it "jumps" out at me.  If you can''t see it on your monitor, try boosting the levels or curves and see if anything shows up.  Also, you have good detail on the wings.  Good work.  Unfortunately, that is one of those details that may not grab the voter on a typical pass, and thus you weren''t "rewarded" for it in the scoring.<br/> <br/>Overall, the shot is good.  It isn''t "WOW" and it isn''t earthshattering.  It is a technically well shot picture.  Looking at your scores, most people seem to think that it falls somewhere in the middle.  So, while I think the composition works, to make it more dramatic, it may have helped to use a tighter crop, or to crop it in an unusual way.  This would help to get the attention of the voters.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to contact me if I need to further elaborate or explain anything I''ve said.<br/> <br/>karmat<br/> <br/></td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, this is a strong picture.  The bird is located roughly on the upper right third and this gives a sense of balance to the shot.  Also, while this location of the subject can sometimes feel out of balance, the fact that the bird is flying "into" the frame helps.  The negative space gives the sense of freedom that one can sometimes associate with birds. Technically, the shot is focus and exposed well.  The colors are simple, so they aren''t distracting, and the bird shows up well on the blue sky.  I do notice a couple of streaks, and after reading your notes, I''m wondering if it is where you cloned out your powerlines.  In normal voting, I''m not sure I would have noticed it, but in studying the picture to critique it, I can''t miss it, and now when I glance at the shot it "jumps" out at me.  If you can''t see it on your monitor, try boosting the levels or curves and see if anything shows up.  Also, you have good detail on the wings.  Good work.  Unfortunately, that is one of those details that may not grab the voter on a typical pass, and thus you weren''t "rewarded" for it in the scoring. Overall, the shot is good.  It isn''t "WOW" and it isn''t earthshattering.  It is a technically well shot picture.  Looking at your scores, most people seem to think that it falls somewhere in the middle.  So, while I think the composition works, to make it more dramatic, it may have helped to use a tighter crop, or to crop it in an unusual way.  This would help to get the attention of the voters. Please feel free to contact me if I need to further elaborate or explain anything I''ve said. karmat ', '2007-02-02 17:12:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3319752, 456391, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, this is an excellent shot.  The bird is located strongly on the lower right thirds and this lends balance and strength to the shot.  Also, the limbs included not only add the "natural" context needed, but the snow adds extra interest to the shot.  <br/> <br/>Technically, this is spot on.  The exposure is such that details show in the plummage, yet the snow isn''t blown out, and you have maintained rich color tones.  The focus on the bird is emphasized by the shallow dof and the lack of focus on the tree.  <br/> <br/>overall, this is an excellent shot that I''m surprised didn''t score higher.  Good work.<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, this is an excellent shot.  The bird is located strongly on the lower right thirds and this lends balance and strength to the shot.  Also, the limbs included not only add the "natural" context needed, but the snow adds extra interest to the shot.   Technically, this is spot on.  The exposure is such that details show in the plummage, yet the snow isn''t blown out, and you have maintained rich color tones.  The focus on the bird is emphasized by the shallow dof and the lack of focus on the tree.   overall, this is an excellent shot that I''m surprised didn''t score higher.  Good work. Karma', '2007-02-02 17:18:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3320057, 456577, 45524, '<td valign="top">Welcome to DPC from the Critique Club, and your first submission to challenges. I have a couple of suggestions for you on your image that might help you with future challenges. First off your subject seems a bit soft then sharpened up a bit, you have lost detail in the birds feathers. I''d suggest with the lens your using to stop it down a bit for a sharper image and bump the ISO up a bit to keep your shutter speed. You also appear to have some CA in the high contrast area in the lower left. Since this was advanced editing that could have been fixed in processing. Your placement of the subject is pretty good. Good luck in future challenges.</td>', 'Welcome to DPC from the Critique Club, and your first submission to challenges. I have a couple of suggestions for you on your image that might help you with future challenges. First off your subject seems a bit soft then sharpened up a bit, you have lost detail in the birds feathers. I''d suggest with the lens your using to stop it down a bit for a sharper image and bump the ISO up a bit to keep your shutter speed. You also appear to have some CA in the high contrast area in the lower left. Since this was advanced editing that could have been fixed in processing. Your placement of the subject is pretty good. Good luck in future challenges.', '2007-02-02 18:05:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3320125, 453377, 69572, '<td valign="top">My first picture with a score over six.  I cant be more happier.  That was my goal for this year.  Going to have to set another now.  Thanks to all that voted</td>', 'My first picture with a score over six.  I cant be more happier.  That was my goal for this year.  Going to have to set another now.  Thanks to all that voted', '2007-02-02 18:16:48.000000', NULL, 0),
